    {
      "id": "a2a4e4d9-acfe-4505-803e-ad5db2fb5d9c",
      "name": "Overview and setup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        0,
        -1200
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 1,
        "width": 1380,
        "height": 1250,
        "content": "## Purpose\nGenerate one video with Fal LTX-2 and keep a recoverable record when a long-running job fails or outlives the local polling budget. Designed for operators who need to distinguish an accepted generation from a network timeout before retrying an expensive request.\n\n## How it works\nA configuration node selects demo, live or resume mode. Live mode submits one prompt to Fal, validates the returned request ID and queue URLs, waits between status checks, and branches on pending, completed or failed states. HTTP 429, server errors and transport errors consume the same bounded polling budget. Completed jobs are checked for provider errors before fetching and validating the video result. Every terminal provider outcome exports a JSON recovery manifest with request URLs and polling history. Invalid configuration stops before any HTTP request.\n\n## Setup\nRun the default demo without credentials: it uses clearly labelled fixtures and generates no video. Choose success, provider_error, timeout or transient to exercise recovery branches. For live mode, create an n8n Header Auth credential: header name Authorization, value Key followed by your Fal API key. Assign it to all three Fal HTTP Request nodes. Check current model pricing, set allowPaidGeneration to true and mode to live. API keys must remain in credentials. Paid Fal usage is separate from this free workflow.\n\n## Recovery and limits\nA submit timeout is ambiguous: automatic POST retries are disabled. Inspect Fal's dashboard before creating another request. To continue a known job, set mode to resume and paste the manifest requestId, status and response URLs into the resume fields. Resume performs reads only. Polling timeout does not cancel a running Fal job or prevent charges. One manual execution handles one job; there is no cross-execution deduplication. Download real media before Fal retention expires and review it before publishing.\n\n## Attribution\nCreated by Shisan Hua, who works on [Flow AI Video](https://www.flowaivideo.org/). This template calls Fal directly; it does not integrate with or modify Flow AI Video's generation endpoints. Demo output URLs are placeholders, never generated assets."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "9c90db84-a058-4994-8333-07302f0c8d9a",
      "name": "1. Explicit mode and spending gate",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        0,
        100
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1320,
        "height": 700,
        "content": "### 1. Explicit mode and spending gate\nDemo is free and offline. Live is opt-in and requires your own Fal credit and credentials. Resume reuses an existing request."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "320e5707-2414-4d40-8e8a-23f75417baeb",
      "name": "2. Preserve the receipt",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1350,
        -30
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 520,
        "height": 700,
        "content": "### 2. Preserve the receipt\nNever retry POST automatically. Unexpected hosts are rejected before credentials can be sent to them. Save the manifest after a terminal outcome."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "a822d0fa-5a06-4300-b69b-c8cba9c7a82e",
      "name": "3. Bounded asynchronous polling",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1900,
        -420
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1100,
        "height": 700,
        "content": "### 3. Bounded asynchronous polling\nWait nodes avoid busy loops. Retry only safe status reads after transient errors. COMPLETED with an error is failure. Timeout stops polling, not Fal inference."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "ad003a27-4cd4-49b9-87bd-1d30a54e2fb5",
      "name": "4. Recoverable delivery",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        3060,
        -460
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 900,
        "height": 700,
        "content": "### 4. Recoverable delivery\nResult URLs must be HTTPS fal.media. This workflow exports a result/recovery manifest; it does not publish to social media. Resume rather than starting a second billable job."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
